    "result_text": "All green. The full test suite (the single `AcceptanceTest` class, plus its helper base classes) compiles and passes, which confirms the generated `OwnerDto` picked up the new `riskFlag` accessor.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` derived field on the owner read model so it is `true` when any of the three risk signals hold, and `false` otherwise.\n\n**1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `riskFlag` boolean read-only property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the existing `bulkSignupWarning`/`capacityWarning` advisory flags), which drives the OpenAPI generator to add `getRiskFlag`/`setRiskFlag` to `OwnerDto`.\n\n**2. `DisposableEmailValidator`** \u2014 Added `isDisposableAdjacent(email)` for the \"disposable-adjacent\" signal: an address whose domain is a *subdomain* of a blocklisted disposable provider (e.g. `inbox.mailinator.com`) \u2014 near enough to a throwaway provider to be risky, but not an exact match (exact matches are already hard-rejected at create time). Factored out a shared `domainOf` helper so the existing `isDisposable` and the new method don't duplicate the parsing logic.\n\n**3. `OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 Added `stampRiskFlag(ownerDto, owner)`, called from the existing `toOwnerDtoWithWarnings` (so both `GET` and create responses carry it, consistent with the other warnings). It ORs the three independent signals:\n- possible duplicate \u2014 the persisted `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()`,\n- disposable-adjacent email \u2014 `DisposableEmailValidator.isDisposableAdjacent`,\n- city over soft capacity \u2014 `countOwnersByCity >= CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD` (the existing soft-capacity constant of 40, reused rather than re-declared).\n\nEach concern stays in the class that owns it: the entity holds the duplicate state, the email validator owns domain rules, and the controller composes the flag from the same threshold constant already used for `capacityWarning`.\n\nOne interpretation I want to flag: I read \"city over its soft capacity\" as reaching or exceeding the soft threshold of 40 (`>= 40`, staying true up to the hard cap of 50), matching how the existing `capacityWarning` defines the soft threshold. If the intended boundary is strictly greater than 40, that's a one-character change (`> `).",
